This dataset reuses or wraps the following work, each Apache-2.0:

- Google Quantum AI, verifiable circuit compilation competition: the
  tools/scripts/chemistry_campaign/scoring.py tool wraps the organizers'
  official scoreinfra equations (dfthc_math.py, reference.py, costs_prepare.py),
  which are loaded by path from the competition data and are not redistributed
  here. https://www.kaggle.com/competitions/google-verifiable-quantum-circuit-compilation
- anazemcev (Artem1410): the PyTorch structure trainer and fixed-word refit code
  that produced the training trajectories and refit reports under results/ were
  vendored unmodified, with their LICENSE and NOTICE, in the pipeline that made
  these results. The code itself is not included; its outputs are.
  https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/anazemcev/vqcc-viberteam-verified-circuits
- Dmitrii Gluzdov: the public (1, 496, 384) factorization used as the starting
  dictionary (not redistributed here).
  https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/dmitriigluzdov/vqcc-femoco-public-factorization

Other entrants' bounds and numbers quoted in README.md are author-reported and
credited there by name.

The negative-results ledger (ledger.csv, ledger.parquet) summarises, in our own words, other entrants'
public reports from Kaggle discussions and notebooks. Each such row names the author by Kaggle display name
and links the original; the numbers in it are the author's (evidence tier author-reported).
